{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e1c2d4-5a6f-4c3b-9d81-2f0a4e6c8b11",
    "name": "ContentMS (HU-211)",
    "description": "Carga y consulta de archivos de contenido estatico en el COS de CMS.\n\n## Antes de empezar\n\n1. Levanta MinIO: `podman-compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yaml up -d`\n2. Arranca el servicio: `PROFILE=minio java -jar target/content-ms-1.0.0.jar`\n   (o `PROFILE=local` para el almacen en memoria, sin contenedores)\n3. En **POST /v1/save-content**, pestana Body, selecciona un archivo en el campo `file`.\n   Tienes uno de ejemplo en `postman/image1.png`. Postman no puede guardar la ruta en la\n   coleccion, asi que este es el unico paso manual.\n\nLos headers `correlation_id` y `request_id` se generan solos con `{{$guid}}` en cada envio.\n\n## Variables\n\n| Variable | Para que |\n|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | Donde escucha el servicio |\n| `partnerId` | El socio; determina el prefijo `partnerId/` en el bucket |\n| `fileName` | Nombre con el que se guarda y se recupera |\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "partnerId",
      "value": "12345",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "fileName",
      "value": "image1.png",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Flujo principal",
      "description": "El ciclo que describe la HU: guardar y recuperar.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /v1/save-content",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('el cuerpo es el responseHeader del HU', () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.returnCode).to.eql('201');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Created');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('devuelve en eco los tres headers del contrato', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('correlation_id')).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('request_id')).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('_p')).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('partnerId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "correlation_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "request_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "_p", "value": "{{partnerId}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "jsonString",
                  "value": "{\"fileName\":\"{{fileName}}\",\"partnerId\":\"{{partnerId}}\"}",
                  "contentType": "application/json",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Campos del HU: fileName (obligatorio) y partnerId (opcional)."
                },
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": null,
                  "description": "Selecciona postman/image1.png u otro archivo admitido. No hace falta declarar el Content-Type: el servicio lo deduce de la extension de fileName."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/save-content",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "save-content"]
            },
            "description": "Guarda el archivo en el COS de CMS bajo `/partnerId/Object`.\n\nEl `partnerId` sale del JSON; si no viene, se usa el header `_p`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /v1/content-loaded",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('devuelve el binario, no un JSON', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseSize).to.be.above(0);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.not.include('application/json');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('el responseHeader del HU viaja como headers', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('returnCode')).to.eql('200');",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('message')).to.eql('OK');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Content-Disposition trae el nombre del archivo', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Disposition'))",
                  "      .to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('fileName'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded?context_url={{partnerId}}%2F{{fileName}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"],
              "query": [{ "key": "context_url", "value": "{{partnerId}}%2F{{fileName}}" }]
            },
            "description": "Devuelve el archivo como binario. Va sin cabeceras: el `context_url` (`<partnerId>/<archivo>`) es su unica entrada, y la respuesta tampoco devuelve `correlation_id`, `request_id` ni `_p`.\n\nUsa **Save Response > Save to a file** para comprobar que es identico al que subiste."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Errores",
      "description": "Cada uno devuelve el cuerpo `errorHeader` / `errorDetail` que define la HU.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "400 - context_url sin prefijo de socio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('forma de error del HU', () => {",
                  "    const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(b.errorHeader.returnCode).to.eql(400);",
                  "    pm.expect(b.errorDetail.code).to.eql('INVALID_OBJECT_PATH');",
                  "    pm.expect(b.errorDetail).to.have.property('errorStack');",
                  "    pm.expect(b.errorDetail.errorDate).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded?context_url={{fileName}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"],
              "query": [{ "key": "context_url", "value": "{{fileName}}" }]
            },
            "description": "El `context_url` debe ser `<partnerId>/<archivo>`. Sin el prefijo del socio no hay clave que componer, asi que se rechaza en vez de buscar en la raiz del bucket."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "400 - falta el parametro context_url",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('codigo MISSING_REQUIRED_PARAMETER', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.code).to.eql('MISSING_REQUIRED_PARAMETER'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "400 - path traversal a otro socio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('la guarda de rutas lo corta', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.code).to.eql('INVALID_OBJECT_PATH'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded?context_url=..%2F99999%2F{{fileName}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"],
              "query": [{ "key": "context_url", "value": "..%2F99999%2F{{fileName}}" }]
            },
            "description": "El `..` va URL-encoded para que ningun cliente lo normalice por el camino.\n\nSin esta guarda, el prefijo `partnerId/` no aislaria nada: cualquiera podria leer los archivos de otro socio del mismo bucket."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "404 - el archivo no existe",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('codigo CONTENT_NOT_FOUND', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.code).to.eql('CONTENT_NOT_FOUND'));",
                  "pm.test('sin stack: un 404 es normal, no un fallo', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.errorStack).to.be.null);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded?context_url={{partnerId}}%2Fno-existe.png",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"],
              "query": [{ "key": "context_url", "value": "{{partnerId}}%2Fno-existe.png" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "404 - archivo de otro socio",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404: bajo el prefijo 99999 no hay nada', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/content-loaded?context_url=99999%2F{{fileName}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "content-loaded"],
              "query": [{ "key": "context_url", "value": "99999%2F{{fileName}}" }]
            },
            "description": "El mismo archivo, pero pedido bajo el prefijo del socio 99999: da 404 porque esa clave no existe.\n\nOjo, esto ya NO prueba aislamiento entre socios: al viajar el partnerId dentro del `context_url`, quien conozca el id de otro socio puede leer sus archivos. El aislamiento tendria que venir de una capa de autorizacion, que aun no existe."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "400 - jsonString malformado",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('codigo INVALID_JSON_STRING', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.code).to.eql('INVALID_JSON_STRING'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "correlation_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "request_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "_p", "value": "{{partnerId}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                { "key": "jsonString", "value": "esto no es json", "type": "text" },
                { "key": "file", "type": "file", "src": null }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/save-content",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "save-content"]
            },
            "description": "Recuerda seleccionar un archivo en `file`, o el fallo sera otro (falta la parte del multipart)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "422 - tipo de contenido no admitido",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422 Unprocessable Entity', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('codigo UNSUPPORTED_CONTENT_TYPE', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().errorDetail.code).to.eql('UNSUPPORTED_CONTENT_TYPE'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "correlation_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "request_id", "value": "{{$guid}}" },
              { "key": "_p", "value": "{{partnerId}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "jsonString",
                  "value": "{\"fileName\":\"nota.txt\",\"partnerId\":\"{{partnerId}}\"}",
                  "contentType": "application/json",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": null,
                  "contentType": "text/plain",
                  "description": "Selecciona postman/nota.txt. La extension .txt no esta en el mapa del servicio, asi que manda el text/plain declarado aqui, que el bucket no admite: 422."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/save-content",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["v1", "save-content"]
            },
            "description": "El bucket solo admite imagenes y PDF. La regla vive en `storage.buckets.cmsContent.allowed-content-types`."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Salud",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /actuator/health",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status UP', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('UP'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["actuator", "health"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
